# One USB command creates legacy 5555 from a cold boot with no AP, no STA and
# no hotspot. Measured 2026-11-27 on the XPLORE 2 (boot_completed 20:46:51).
#
# The Wi-Fi radio state is irrelevant: adbd writes service.adb.tcp.port
# itself, so this bypasses the AdbDebuggingManager toggle gate entirely.

# 1. After the cold boot, with Wi-Fi disabled and the laptop AP down:
$ adb shell 'date; getprop service.adb.tcp.port; settings get global adb_wifi_enabled; cmd wifi status | head -1'
Fri Nov 27 20:46:50 CET 2026
(empty)
0
Wifi is disabled
$ adb shell 'ip -4 -o addr show wlan0; ip -4 -o addr show ap0'
(no output: no STA, no hotspot)
$ adb shell 'cat /proc/net/tcp /proc/net/tcp6 | awk ...'
5555_listeners=0

# 2. The entire bootstrap:
$ adb tcpip 5555
restarting in TCP mode port: 5555

# adbd restarts; the property is visible again in about a second.
$ adb shell 'getprop service.adb.tcp.port'
5555
$ adb shell 'cat /proc/net/tcp /proc/net/tcp6 | awk ...'
5555_listeners=1

# The radio came up by itself in this first run; step 3 repeats the
# measurement with it explicitly off, so the result does not depend on it.

# 3. Re-measured with the radio explicitly off (no wlan0, no ap0):
$ adb shell 'svc wifi disable'
$ adb shell 'cmd wifi status | head -1; settings get global adb_wifi_enabled'
Wifi is disabled
0
$ adb tcpip 5555
restarting in TCP mode port: 5555
property_visible_s=1.016
$ adb shell 'getprop service.adb.tcp.port; ... listener count ...; cmd wifi status | head -1; settings get global adb_wifi_enabled'
5555
5555_listeners=1
Wifi is disabled
0

# 4. The cable is now optional. Later in the same boot the phone hosted a
#    5 GHz P2P group and adb rode it with the toggle still off:
$ adb shell 'am start -n org.phonelink.p2pprobe/.MainActivity --ei freq 5180 --es ssid DIRECT-KL-5G --es psk <redacted> --ei hold 240000'
createGroup: success
group owner: true
group interface: p2p-p2p0-0
$ nmcli device wifi connect DIRECT-KL-5G password <redacted> ifname wlp110s0
Device 'wlp110s0' successfully activated
$ adb connect 192.168.49.1:5555
connected to 192.168.49.1:5555
$ adb -s 192.168.49.1:5555 shell 'echo P2P_OK; id -u; getprop service.adb.tcp.port; settings get global adb_wifi_enabled'
P2P_OK
2000
5555
0

# Limits:
# - the property is volatile: the next reboot clears it, so this command is a
#   per-boot bootstrap, not persistence;
# - the toggle is never involved (0 throughout), so this is legacy adbd, not
#   Wireless debugging;
# - the USB host is the adb client the user already has; no AP, router, second
#   radio or extra device is needed;
# - without any USB host, the bootstrap still needs a temporary STA (Keeper
#   re-pins 5555 in ~17 s) or root.
